Uploading VSCode Project to GitHub

To upload a VSCode project to GitHub, follow these steps:
    Initialize a Git Repository: Open your project in VSCode and open the terminal. 
    Run the following command to initialize a Git repository: git init
        git init
    Add Files to the Repository: Add all your project files to the repository using: 
        git add .
    Commit the Changes: Commit your changes with a message: 
        git commit -m "Initial commit"
    Create a Repository on GitHub: Go to GitHub and create a new repository. Do not initialize it with a README, .gitignore, or license.
    Add Remote Repository: Copy the URL of your new GitHub repository and add it as a remote in your local repository: 
        git remote add origin <repository URL>
    Push to GitHub: Push your local repository to GitHub: 
        git push -u origin master

Example
# Initialize a new Git repository
    git init
# Add all files to the staging area
    git add
# Commit the changes with a message
    git commit -m "Initial commit"
# Add the remote repository URL
    git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/your-repo.git
# Push the changes to the master branch on GitHub
    git push -u origin master


