TO UPDATE CHANGES:
1. Initialize Git Repository
    Click the Source Control icon (or press Ctrl + Shift + G).
    Click Initialize Repository to start tracking changes.

2. Commit Your Changes
    In the Source Control panel, select files to stage (click the + icon).
    Enter a commit message in the text box.
    Click the checkmark (✔) to commit.

3. Publish to GitHub
    In the Source Control panel, click Publish to GitHub.
    Choose Public or Private repository.
    Select files you want to upload and confirm.
    VS Code will create the repo on GitHub and push your code.

4. Push Future Changes
When you make updates:
    Stage changes (+ icon).
    Commit with a message.
    Click the three dots (…) → Push.

5. Verify on GitHub



